naga: spv-in: only skip the entry point wrappers' fake function ids

Found by the naga `spv_parser` fuzz target: `index out of bounds: the len is
0 but the index is 3` at `front/spv/mod.rs` `patch_statements`
(`fun_parameter_sampling[i as usize] |= flags`).

The entry point wrappers call their functions through fake ids `!0, !1, ..`
(one per entry point), and the patching pass in `parse` skips them with
`fun_id > !(functions.len() as u32)`. That threshold counts functions, not
entry points, so it also skipped real functions whose ids lie just below
`u32::MAX` (the fuzzer's module: no entry points, a function with id
0xFFFFFFFD). The skipped function was never moved into the new arena; its
stale handle aliased another function's, `patch_function`'s
`lookup.handle == h` search then took that function's (empty) parameter
sampling flags, and indexing them panicked. Now:

- the skip compares against `!(entry_points.len())`, i.e. exactly the fake
  ids;
- a real function whose id collides with a fake id is refused with
  `Error::InvalidId` before the wrappers are built (the ids must be below the
  header's bound anyway).

Regression tests in `naga/tests/naga/spirv_malformed.rs` (added by
fix-naga-spv-malformed-module-panics.patch).

Not fixed upstream as of 110b588.
Upstream: none found; the open umbrella issue gfx-rs/wgpu#7687 does not list
this site.

diff --git a/naga/src/front/spv/mod.rs b/naga/src/front/spv/mod.rs
index 48cf4e0..b9891d2 100644
--- a/naga/src/front/spv/mod.rs
+++ b/naga/src/front/spv/mod.rs
@@ -1817,6 +1817,21 @@ impl<I: Iterator<Item = u32>> Frontend<I> {
             module.upgrade_atomics(&self.upgrade_atomics)?;
         }
 
+        // The entry point wrappers call their functions through the fake ids
+        // `!0, !1, ..`, one per entry point, and the patching below skips those
+        // ids. A real function with an id in that range would be skipped too
+        // and keep a stale handle into the old function arena.
+        let fake_ids_above = !(self.deferred_entry_points.len() as u32);
+        if let Some(id) = self
+            .lookup_function
+            .keys()
+            .copied()
+            .filter(|&id| id > fake_ids_above)
+            .min()
+        {
+            return Err(Error::InvalidId(id));
+        }
+
         // Do entry point specific processing after all functions are parsed so that we can
         // cull unused problematic builtins of gl_PerVertex.
         for (ep, fun_id) in mem::take(&mut self.deferred_entry_points) {
@@ -1830,7 +1845,11 @@ impl<I: Iterator<Item = u32>> Frontend<I> {
             nodes.reverse(); // we need dominated first
             let mut functions = module.functions.take();
             for fun_id in nodes {
-                if fun_id > !(functions.len() as u32) {
+                // The fake ids are `!0..=!(entry_points.len() - 1)`. Comparing
+                // against the number of functions instead also skipped real
+                // functions with ids just below the fake ones, which kept stale
+                // handles that alias other functions in the new arena.
+                if fun_id > !(module.entry_points.len() as u32) {
                     // skip all the fake IDs registered for the entry points
                     continue;
                 }
